grep -v -x -f web_only.txt total_resolving.txt > non_web_targets.txt


Step 1: Services aur Open Ports Find Karna (Naabu)
Kyunki in par HTTP (80/443) nahi chal raha, humein pata lagana hoga ki aakhir in par chal kya raha hai. Hum Naabu ka use karke top 1000 common ports scan karenge.

Bash
naabu -l non_web_targets.txt -top-ports 1000 -c 50 -rate 2000 -silent -o open_ports.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command check karegi ki kya kisi server par FTP (21), SSH (22), MySQL (3306), Redis (6379), ya MongoDB (27017) jaise ports khule hue hain. Results open_ports.txt mein subdomain:port format mein save honge.

Step 2: Automated Misconfiguration Testing (Nuclei)
Ab jo ports khule mile hain, humein un par default passwords ya known network vulnerabilities check karni hain. Nuclei ka network/ module iske liye best hai.

Bash
nuclei -l open_ports.txt -t network/ -tags default-login,misconfig -o network_bugs.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command bina brute-force kiye check karegi ki kya kisi FTP par anonymous login on hai, ya kisi database par bina password ke login ho raha hai. Agar koi bug milta hai, toh wo network_bugs.txt mein save ho jayega.

Step 3: Subdomain Takeover Check Karna (Nuclei)
In "non-web" subdomains mein se bohot saare subdomains aise honge jin par koi port open nahi hoga aur wo DNS level par dead honge (jaise kisi delete ho chuke AWS S3 bucket ya GitHub page ko point kar rahe hon). Yeh Subdomain Takeover ke liye perfect targets hain.

Bash
nuclei -l non_web_targets.txt -t takeovers/ -o takeovers_found.txt
Kyun kiya? Yeh command check karegi ki kya koi DNS record kisi aisi third-party service ko point kar raha hai jise aap claim karke company ka subdomain hijack kar sakte hain. Yeh bug bounty mein P2/P3 level ka critical bug hota hai.

